title: Inter-Party Relationships
new-page: true
view-if: year <= 1932 and inter_party_relationships_timer <= 0
tags: party_affairs
is-card: true
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; inter_party_relationships_timer = 6;
card-image: img/weimar_coalition_2.jpg
max-visits: 12
#subtitle: Building relations with the other political parties of Germany.

= Inter-Party Relationships

Whilst our ultimate goal is revolution and deposition of the republic, it would not be wise to ignore the other parties entirely in the time being.

- @spd: Work towards repairing relationships with the Social Democratic Party.
- @center: Try to reach out to the Catholic Center Party.
- @liberals: Attempt contact with members of the left-liberal German Democratic Party.
- @kpd_alone: The KPD can stand alone for now.
- @easy_discard


@spd
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; spd_inter_party_seen += 1
go-to: spd_blutmai if blutmai = 1; spd_1 if blutmai = 0 and spd_coalition_success = 0 and (spd_relation < 40 or spd_rectified_history = 1); spd_rectification_of_history if spd_relation >= 40 and spd_rectified_history = 0; spd_2 if spd_coalition_success = 1 and spd_rectified_history = 1

@spd_1
on-arrival: spd_relation += 6*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if spd_inter_party_seen <= 1; center_dissent += 2; z_relation -= 2; ddp_relation -= 2

The Social Democrats remain deeply suspicious of our overtures, pointing to official Comintern rhetoric that labels them "social fascists." Nevertheless, tactical connections and anti-fascist unity begin to build at the grassroots level and on shop floors.

@spd_rectification_of_history

A major barrier to lasting cooperation with the SPD is our history of bloody conflict dating back to 1918 and 1919. Our rank-and-file has never forgiven Gustav Noske, the SPD minister who ordered the violent suppression of the Spartacist uprising, nor the murders of Rosa Luxemburg and Karl Liebknecht.

To move toward genuine United Front actions, our central committee demands that the SPD leadership acknowledge Noske's crimes, disavow past anti-worker violence, and honor Luxemburg and Liebknecht.

- @yes_history: Demand a formal apology and historical accountability from the SPD.
- @no_history: Set aside past grievances to prioritize immediate joint action.

@yes_history
on-arrival: left_dissent -= 6; left_strength += 5; center_dissent += 5; spd_rectified_history = 1; z_relation -= 5; ddp_relation -= 4; spd_relation += 8*(1-dissent)

We insist that the SPD publicly acknowledge the betrayals of 1919. While moderate SPD executives react with anger, left-wing Social Democrats and rank-and-file trade unionists push their leadership to concede, opening a path toward historic reconciliation.

@no_history
on-arrival: spd_relation -= 3; left_dissent += 4

We drop our demands for a formal apology in the name of immediate tactical flexibility. Many in our radical wing accuse the leadership of selling out the martyrs of 1919, while the SPD leadership remains wary.


@spd_2
on-arrival: spd_relation += 8*(1 - dissent); communist_coalition += 1 if spd_inter_party_seen <= 1; center_dissent += 2; z_relation -= 3

Following successful joint initiatives and cooperation, SPD organizers and rank-and-file workers are far more receptive to working alongside us.

@spd_blutmai
on-arrival: spd_relation += 2*(1 - dissent); left_dissent += 3; center_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; neorevisionist_dissent += 3; labor_strength -= 3

After the police massacre of May Day 1929 under Berlin Police Chief Otto Zörgiebel, reconciliation with the Social Democratic leadership is extraordinarily difficult. Fury sweeps through the party: every non-conciliator faction sees their dissent rise significantly, and the Conciliators lose considerable political strength for advocating cooperation with police executioners.

@center
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; z_seen += 1
go-to: center_refuse if z_seen < 2; center_dialogue if z_seen >= 2

@center_refuse
on-arrival: left_dissent += 1

The Catholic Center Party flatly refuses to take our meeting, dismissing our delegates as anti-clerical subversives. We will need to make another attempt before they even consider opening dialogue.

@center_dialogue
on-arrival: z_relation += 2*(1 - dissent)
go-to: center_op if z_in_government = 1 and spd_in_government = 0 and chancellor != "Brüning"; center_coalition if spd_in_government = 1 and z_in_government = 1; center_bruning if chancellor = "Brüning"

@center_op
on-arrival: z_relation += 2*(1 - dissent)

Having established basic contact on our second attempt, the Catholic Center Party reluctantly permits limited communication in the Reichstag during opposition maneuvers.

@center_coalition
on-arrival: z_relation += 2*(1 - dissent)

While the Center Party sits in government, ongoing dialogue remains extremely guarded and strictly limited to parliamentary mechanics.

@center_bruning
on-arrival: z_relation += 1*(1 - dissent)

Under Chancellor Brüning's semi-autocratic emergency decrees, reaching out to the Center Party yields almost no further results.

@liberals
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; ddp_seen += 1
go-to: ddp_refuse if ddp_seen < 3; ddp_dialogue if ddp_seen >= 3

@ddp_refuse

The [+ ddp_name +] rejects our outreach outright, viewing us as total enemies of the republic. They refuse to grant an audience to red delegates at this time.

@ddp_dialogue
on-arrival: ddp_relation += 2*(1 - dissent)

Finally, on our third attempt, key members of the [+ ddp_name +] agree to sit down with our delegates. While fundamentally opposed to proletarian revolution, tentative dialogue regarding constitutional rights and anti-fascist defense can now proceed at a very slow pace.

@kpd_alone

Whether due to revolutionary purity or tactical necessity, we make no overtures to bourgeois or reformist parties at this time, relying solely on our own vanguard organization.

- @return: Continue...